{"step_index":405,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T19:01:45Z","input_tokens":2557,"cache_read_tokens":173064,"output_tokens":6088,"thinking":"Examining the code for the evidence indexer involves verifying the database table creation with its indexes and ensuring the implementation of two-pass trace correlation. This correlation strategy necessitates grouping log entries by trace ID, with a fallback mechanism when the trace ID is unavailable. The initial pass must check specified fields to identify related evidence records.\n\n\nThe initial pass parses trace data, extracting user identifiers and applying lookups. The second pass analyzes extracted data, determining the state of the resource based on specific conditions such as row counts or HTTP status. This information is then inserted into the evidence records database.\n\nAnalysis will now extend to parsing records from evidence files, capturing resource identifiers. Anonymized analytics records require correlation against system activity logs to associate them with deletion requests using event timestamps. These associations are then used to update user identifiers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nZero-token local evidence indexer for Northstar Shop Deletion Audit dataset.\\nCorrelates trace events across logs and records into SQLite cache/northstar.db.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport csv\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nimport sqlite3\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\n\\nKV_REGEX = re.compile(r'(\\\\w+)=(?:\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"|(\\\\S+))')\\n\\n\\ndef _clean_str(val: Any) -> Optional[str]:\\n    if val is None:\\n        return None\\n    s = str(val).strip()\\n    if not s or s.lower() in (\\\"null\\\", \\\"none\\\"):\\n        return None\\n    return s\\n\\n\\ndef _parse_iso_ts(ts_str: Any) -> Optional[datetime]:\\n    if not ts_str:\\n        return None\\n    s = str(ts_str).strip()\\n    if not s or s.lower() in (\\\"null\\\", \\\"none\\\"):\\n        return None\\n    try:\\n        return datetime.fromisoformat(s.replace(\\\"Z\\\", \\\"+00:00\\\"))\\n    except Exception:\\n        return None\\n\\n\\ndef index_unstructured_evidence(\\n    evidence_dir: Path = Path(\\\"dataset/evidence\\\"),\\n    conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None,\\n) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Parse files in logs/ and records/, perform two-pass trace correlation,\\n    correlate anonymized analytics from system_activity, and populate evidence_records.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    evidence_path = Path(evidence_dir)\\n    close_conn = False\\n\\n    if conn is None:\\n        db_path = Path(\\\"cache/northstar.db\\\")\\n        db_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n        conn = sqlite3.connect(db_path)\\n        close_conn = True\\n\\n    try:\\n        # 1. Table Schema\\n        conn.execute(\\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS evidence_records (\\n                file_id TEXT,\\n                captured_at TEXT,\\n                system_id TEXT,\\n                resource_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n                verified_state TEXT,       -- 'ABSENT', 'PRESENT', 'ANONYMIZED', 'REDACTED'\\n                user_id TEXT,\\n                email TEXT\\n            );\\\n<truncated 22694 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Pavan\\\\hackerrank-orchestrate-october26\\\\src\\\\evidence_indexer.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
